From: skrimix <skrimix.git@fastmail.org>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: acknowledge power role and PD hard reset notifications

The Pad 2 ADSP charger firmware sends Oplus notifications 0x7d
(BC_POWER_ROLE_STATUS) and 0x7f (PD_CONNECT_HARD_RESET) during boot,
which the driver logs as unknown notification errors. In the Oplus
kernel, 0x7d only republishes the USB power role to its charging
policy, which Linux gets from UCSI, and 0x7f only adjusts reverse
charging, which the stock device tree does not configure.

Acknowledge both alongside the other informational Oplus events.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -137,6 +137,8 @@ enum qcom_battmgr_variant {
 #define NOTIF_OPLUS_UFCS_PWR_INFO_READY 0x77
 #define NOTIF_OPLUS_BATTERY_RESET_START 0x78
 #define NOTIF_OPLUS_PD_SOURCECAP_DONE 0x79
+#define NOTIF_OPLUS_POWER_ROLE_STATUS 0x7d
+#define NOTIF_OPLUS_PD_HARD_RESET 0x7f
 
 #define OPLUS_USB_VOOCPHY_ENABLE 16
 #define OPLUS_PPS_READ_BUFFER 0x10004
@@ -3013,6 +3015,8 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_notification(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 	case NOTIF_OPLUS_UFCS_DISABLE_MOS:
 	case NOTIF_OPLUS_UFCS_PWR_INFO_READY:
 	case NOTIF_OPLUS_BATTERY_RESET_START:
+	case NOTIF_OPLUS_POWER_ROLE_STATUS:
+	case NOTIF_OPLUS_PD_HARD_RESET:
 		/* Handled / acknowledged proprietary fast charging events */
 		dev_info(battmgr->dev, "OnePlus charging notification: %#x\n", notification);
 		break;
